      "observed": "The FCC crystal network connects to FCC1.5 (PE6) and FCC1.37 (PE7), rather than its PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. The NAVC HSE crystal nets have no NAVC1 connection; NAVC1.5 (PH0) and NAVC1.6 (PH1) instead connect to separate capacitors to ground.",
      "expected": "The stated 25 MHz HSE crystals should connect to each MCU's HSE oscillator input and output pins (PH0 and PH1).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(NAVC1-PH0)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU's HSE crystal is correctly connected, so the intended external clock source will not operate; the processors may fall back to another clock source or fail clock-dependent operation.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows major connectivity faults: both MCUs' supply pins are unconnected, FCC UART3 is routed to VCAP pins, and the HSE crystal networks do not reach the MCUs' oscillator pins. These deviations prevent the board from behaving as specified."
}

